\section{Caveats}{
\itemize{
\item Trust numerator/denominator on basis count rows and fraction on basis intensity rows: each cell rounds the other (ModificationOccupancyCell).
\item entity_index cannot be zipped with protein_group_name's accessions: an entity with no sites is dropped from the cell.
\item A malformed cell is refused by mzLib (FormatException), named in failed_fields as count_occupancy or intensity_occupancy, and gives no rows.
\item A truncated cell keeps its complete sites with cell_is_truncated true; truncated_cell_count counts every cut cell, including those with no rows.
\item offset and limit count GROUPS; a group with no modified sites gives no rows.
\item Many files: \code{--paths-stdin} reads the list in ONE process, \code{--threads} at a time, into one long table with source_index and source_path first. The output does not depend on \code{--threads} (a tested property); the default of 1 is a memory choice, since every reader materialises the whole file.
}
}
\section{Performance}{
Every call starts one bridge process, which costs a .NET start-up before any work. This bulk form pays it once for the whole list, which is the reason it exists: never loop the one-path function over many files.
}
